Day 6 of hashtag#60DayClaudeChallenge 🚀
Today I used Claude AI to optimize my resume for ATS (Applicant Tracking System) — and the results were eye-opening.
My ATS score jumped from 52/100 → 84/100 with just structural and keyword changes.
Here's what I fixed:
✅ Removed tab-based layout and switched to a clean single-column format for accurate ATS parsing
✅ Added a Professional Summary — ATS ranks resumes higher when keywords appear near the top
✅ Used standard section headings — Professional Summary, Education, Technical Skills, Experience, Projects, Certifications
✅ Replaced weak descriptions with strong action verbs — Designed, Built, Identified, Delivered
✅ Added quantified metrics to every bullet — 30% engagement, 100+ records, 15+ bugs fixed
✅ Organized skills into labelled categories — Languages, Web Development, Database, Tools
A resume isn't just about listing skills.
It's about presenting them in a way that both ATS and recruiters can easily read.
One structural change = a better shot at getting shortlisted. 🎯
